title: $:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/doc/architecture
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<$transclude $tiddler="$:/plugins/rimir/doc-template/templates/page">
<$fill $name="body">

!! Layers

# ''Storage'' — plain TW tiddlers under `knowledge/…`, tagged `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/note`, with `kn.tier` / `kn.type` fields and free-form body.
# ''Resolution'' — namespace plugin handles `[[Foo]]` resolution via its 9-stage pipeline (literal → alias → mount → pseudo → walk-up → unresolved). The app enables walk-up + aliases + pseudo-expansion + self-prefix on install.
# ''App shell'' — appify framework. App declared at `$:/plugins/rimir/knowledge-app/apps/knowledge` with channels `area note` and the `topbar-main` layout (topbar row + full-width main).
# ''Navigation'' — `apps/knowledge-main` renders a multi-select filter chip strip (tier + type) above a full-width `<$mindmap>` widget. The mindmap consumes `views/knowledge-mindmap-view`, which binds the `knowledge-tree` producer in forest mode with `collapse-below-depth: 1` (area roots expanded, descendants collapsed initially).
# ''Preview'' — built into the mindmap (right edge of the canvas). The mindmap's `mm.preview-top-template` extension point pulls in `templates/preview-top.tid`, which surfaces the `kn-type-pill` interactive popup above the body. Below the body, the mindmap's built-in backlinks/outgoing panel renders using `ns-backlinks` / `ns-forwardlinks` (configured via `mm.backlinks-filter` / `mm.outgoing-filter` on the view tiddler).

!! Channels

| Channel | Set by | Read by |
|`area` | Topbar area pills | Capture modal (target area for new notes) |
|`note` | Mindmap node-select (via `mindmap-title-for-op` operator in `onSelectActions`) | Mindmap preview pane internally — exposed for any external consumers |

!! Filter chip state

| State tiddler | Format | Toggled by |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/filter/tiers` | TW title list | `procedures/filter-chips.tid` tier chips |
|`$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/filter/types` | TW title list | `procedures/filter-chips.tid` type chips |

Empty list = no constraint on that axis. The mindmap reproduces on changes via the `node-filter-watch` arg on the view tiddler.

!! Filter operators

* `[<title>knowledge-has-broken-ref[]]` — input title if its body contains at least one unresolved `[[…]]`, else nothing.
* `[<source>kn-active-node-filter[]]` — filters the input set down to tiddlers whose `kn.tier` × `kn.type` match the active chip selection (empty axis = unconstrained). Wired into the mindmap via the view's `mm.args.node-filter`.

!! Filter functions

`filters/helpers.tid` exposes the diagnostic functions (currently no live UI consumer, but they're useful from the LLM tools and external probes):

* `\function knowledge.notes()` — all notes via the system tag
* `\function knowledge.orphans()` — notes with zero `ns-backlinks`
* `\function knowledge.dead-ends()` — notes with zero `ns-forwardlinks`
* `\function knowledge.stubs()` — notes whose body is shorter than the configured threshold
* `\function knowledge.broken()` — notes whose body contains an unresolved `[[ref]]`

!! Custom pseudo

`pseudo/_index.js` (module-type `rimir-ns-pseudo`) — `_index` segment resolves to `index` or `README` if either exists under the preceding prefix. Use inside an absolute ref like `[[knowledge/topics/foo/_index]]`.

!! Type-specific forms

Each note type (defined in `config/types.tid`) can opt into two extension points:

# ''Capture form'' — `forms/capture-<type>`. Transcluded inside the quick-capture modal between the type select and the body textarea (only when the chosen type has a matching tiddler). Inputs bind to dedicated state tiddlers under `$:/state/rimir/knowledge-app/capture/<type>/<field>` so they survive type-switching and don't collide with the generic title/body state.
# ''Render form'' — `forms/render-<type>`. Currently ''orphan'' — the previous `views/note.tid` (still on disk) transcluded `forms/render-<noteType>` above the body. With the mindmap-driven preview, render-forms are not yet wired in. Re-introduction is planned via a custom `mm.preview-body-template` that dispatches on `kn.type` before falling through to the default body template.

Helpers shared between the two halves of a type live in `forms/<type>-helpers.tid` and are pulled in via `\import`.

!! Mindmap integration

The whole navigation + preview surface lives inside `$mindmap`:

* ''Producer'' — `knowledge-tree` (shipped from `rimir/mindmap`), forest mode (`include-areas-root: yes`). Reads area tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/knowledge-app/area` and walks `knowledge/<area>/…` titles.
* ''Initial collapse'' — `collapse-below-depth: 1` marks every node deeper than the area root as `core:collapsed=true` in the BASE MDOM. The overlay (per-widget state) overrides on user expand, so chosen branches stay open across reloads.
* ''Node filter'' — `[all[shadows+tiddlers]prefix[knowledge/]] +[kn-active-node-filter[]]` runs against the chip state. The producer prunes the tree bottom-up with ancestor preservation: a node survives if its `core:tiddler` matches OR any descendant matches.
* ''Selection wiring'' — `onSelectActions` on the widget calls `<$action-statewrap-set channel="note" value={{{ [<nodeId>mindmap-title-for-op[]] }}}/>`. The `mindmap-title-for-op` operator (in `rimir/mindmap`) dispatches across producers' `titleForOp` functions.
* ''Type pill'' — `templates/preview-top.tid` is bound via `mm.preview-top-template`. It transcludes the existing `kn-type-pill` procedure with `interactive=yes`, surfacing the 15-type popup grouped core / entity / structural above the body.
* ''Backlinks/Outgoing'' — built into the mindmap preview (mindmap ≥ 0.2.29). The knowledge-app view overrides the default `backlinks[]` / `links[]` operators with `ns-backlinks[]` / `ns-forwardlinks[]` so namespace-resolved references are counted. Clicking an entry re-selects that node in the canvas.

</$fill>
</$transclude>
